<speak>
From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your daily briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">21022026</say-as>.
<break time="1s"/>
The United States Supreme Court struck down <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">175</say-as> billion dollars in tariffs imposed by President Trump, ruling six to three that he exceeded his constitutional authority over trade. Hours later, Trump signed a new <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">10</say-as> percent global tariff under a <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">1974</say-as> statute that has never been tested in court. Congress must vote to extend the duties within <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">150</say-as> days, setting up another showdown over presidential trade power.
<break time="900ms"/>
In politics.<break time="400ms"/>
Washington is negotiating a nuclear deal that would let Saudi Arabia enrich uranium, without the enhanced inspections imposed on the United Arab Emirates. The deal reaches Congress while the administration simultaneously demands <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="iːˈrɑːn">Iran</phoneme> abandon its own enrichment programme.
<break time="600ms"/>
Poland became the first NATO ally to withdraw from the Ottawa landmine ban, calling mines essential to defending its borders with Russia and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="bʲɪlɐˈrus">Belarus</phoneme>. Ukraine has also begun leaving the <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">1997</say-as> treaty, signalling that Russia's invasion is unravelling post-Cold War arms control.
<break time="600ms"/>
In <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈtyɾcije">Turkey</phoneme>, <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">30</say-as> police officers detained <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈdɔʏtʃə ˈvɛlə">Deutsche Welle</phoneme> correspondent <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="aliˈdʒan uluˈdaː">Alican Uludağ</phoneme> in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈaŋkaɾa">Ankara</phoneme> on charges of insulting the president. The broadcaster's director general called the charges baseless and demanded his immediate release.
<break time="900ms"/>
In conflict and security.<break time="400ms"/>
Britain refused to let the United States use two of its military bases for strikes on <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="iːˈrɑːn">Iran</phoneme>, warning the action could breach international law. The refusal narrows American basing options as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɛˈhɾɑːn">Tehran</phoneme> says a draft nuclear deal could be ready within days.
<break time="900ms"/>
On the economy.<break time="400ms"/>
A Financial Times investigation found <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">48</say-as> shell companies exported <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">90</say-as> billion dollars in sanctioned Russian crude through <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌɑːzɛɾbɑɪˈdʒɑːn">Azerbaijan</phoneme> and Dubai. The network handled over <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">80</say-as> percent of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="rɐsˈnjeftʲ">Rosneft</phoneme>'s seaborne exports, revealing sanctions evasion on an industrial scale.
<break time="600ms"/>
South Korea's benchmark stock index closed above <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">5800</say-as> for the first time, a day after former President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="juːn sʌk jʌl">Yoon Suk Yeol</phoneme> received a life sentence for his martial law attempt. Goldman Sachs forecasts <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">120</say-as> percent earnings growth for Korean equities this year, led by semiconductor firms.
<break time="900ms"/>
In science.<break time="400ms"/>
NASA announced that four astronauts will fly around the Moon on March sixth aboard Artemis Two, the first crewed mission beyond Earth orbit since <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">1972</say-as>. A successful flyby would clear the path for a crewed lunar landing on Artemis Three.
<break time="900ms"/>
In technology.<break time="400ms"/>
Russia imported <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">125</say-as> million dollars in drones from Thailand in eleven months, an eightfold surge. Bloomberg traced the supply chain to Chinese manufacturers shipping through Thai intermediaries, with the dual-use drones ending up on the Ukrainian front line.
<break time="1s"/>
That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.
</speak>
